## psc/cmd/migrate.pengu — `psc migrate` (F2: migración mecánica de sintaxis).
##
## Reescribe solo transformaciones **mecánicas**: grafías que producen el
## mismo AST y, por tanto, el mismo código en los dos backends.
##
## | Antes | Después |
## |---|---|
## | `list of T` | `vector of T` |
## | `slice of T` | `span of T` |
## | `map of K to V` | `map of K, V` |
## | `nasci` / `mori` / `imago` | `born` / `die` / `mirror` |
## | `namespace` | `regnum` |
##
## Lo que **no** hace, por necesitar semántica nueva o resolución de tipos:
## `umap`/`set`/`uset`, la retirada de `derive`, los ~66 identificadores que
## pasan a ser reservados (`result`, `span`, `set`, `map`, `unique`) y los
## 87 `declare` de la FFI. Esas fases tienen su propio ciclo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Cada edición posee su texto de reemplazo; `free_edits` lo libera.

import std.archivum
import std.builder
import std.spark

import psc.cli.args as cliargs
import psc.sema.names as npool
import psc.source as psource
import psc.token as pstoken
import psc.lexer as pslexer
import psc.lexer_state as psstate
import psc.diag_compat as diag_compat
import psc.ast.kind as pskind
import psc.ast.node as psast
import psc.parse.api as papi
import psc.parse.state as pstate

insignia psc_cmd_migrate_

## Una edición: reemplaza los bytes `[start, end)` por `text`.
##
## ## Memoria
## `text` es owned; liberar con `free_edit`.
rune MigrateEdit derive Nexus:
    ## Offset inclusivo.
    start as int
    ## Offset exclusivo.
    end as int
    ## Texto de reemplazo.
    text as string

## Resultado de migrar un texto.
##
## ## Memoria
## `text` es owned; `ok` es falso si el archivo no se pudo parsear.
rune MigrateOutcome derive Nexus:
    ## Texto migrado (copia owned).
    text as string
    ## Número de ediciones aplicadas.
    changes as int
    ## `true` si el archivo se pudo parsear.
    ok as bool

## Ayuda.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna.
weave print_help into void:
    calling spark.println with "Usage: psc migrate [PATHS...] [options]"
    calling spark.println with "  --check       no escribir; exit 1 si cambiaría algo"
    calling spark.println with "  --diff        mostrar cada edición (línea y columna)"
    calling spark.println with "  --verbose     listar los archivos tocados"
    calling spark.println with "  --help"
    calling spark.println with ""
    calling spark.println with "Transformaciones: list of -> vector of, slice of -> span of,"
    calling spark.println with "map of K to V -> map of K, V, nasci/mori/imago/namespace -> born/die/mirror/regnum."

## Copia owned.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string owned.
weave copy with s as string into string:
    return calling npool.copy_string with s

## `true` si `s` termina en `suffix`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(suffix).
weave ends_with with s as string, suffix as string into bool:
    var n as int is s length
    var m as int is suffix length
    if m > n:
        return false
    return (s at (n - m) to n) == suffix

## Añade una edición con copia owned del texto.
##
## ## Memoria
## Asigna el reemplazo.
weave add_edit with es as ref to vector of MigrateEdit, start as int, end as int, text as string into void:
    var e as MigrateEdit is with start is start, end is end, text is calling copy with text
    calling es.push with e

## Índice del primer token cuyo `start` es `>= off`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(log n).
weave token_index_at with tokens as vector of Token, off as int into int:
    var lo as int is 0
    var hi as int is tokens.len
    while lo < hi:
        var mid as int is (lo + hi) / 2
        if (tokens at mid).start < off:
            set lo is mid + 1
        else:
            set hi is mid
    return lo

## Ordena las ediciones por `start` (inserción; son pocas por archivo).
##
## ## Memoria
## Mueve valores; no asigna.
weave sort_edits with es as ref to vector of MigrateEdit into void:
    var i as int is 1
    while i < es->len:
        var j as int is i
        while j > 0:
            var prev as MigrateEdit is es at (j - 1)
            var cur as MigrateEdit is es at j
            if prev.start <= cur.start:
                break
            set es at (j - 1) is cur
            set es at j is prev
            set j is j - 1
        set i is i + 1

## Renombra la palabra que abre un nodo de tipo (`list` -> `vector`).
##
## `head` es el offset del nodo; el token debe empezar exactamente ahí.
##
## ## Memoria
## Añade la edición si hace falta.
weave rename_head with text as string, tokens as vector of Token, head as int, from_word as string, to_word as string, es as ref to vector of MigrateEdit into void:
    var ti as int is calling token_index_at with tokens, head
    if ti >= tokens.len:
        return
    var t as Token is tokens at ti
    if t.start != head:
        return
    if (text at t.start to t.end) != from_word:
        return
    calling add_edit with es, t.start, t.end, to_word

## Convierte el separador de un `map of K to V` en una coma.
##
## Usa el AST: el separador es el primer `to` entre el final del tipo clave y
## el principio del tipo valor. Así los mapas anidados (`map of map of a to b
## to c`) no se confunden y `result of T to E` no se toca.
##
## ## Memoria
## Añade la edición si hace falta.
weave convert_map_sep with ast as ref to PsAst, tokens as vector of Token, nid as int, es as ref to vector of MigrateEdit into void:
    var node as PsNode is ast->nodes at nid
    if node.child_count < 2:
        return
    var kc as int is ast->children at node.first_child
    var vc as int is ast->children at (node.first_child + 1)
    if kc <= 0 or vc <= 0:
        return
    var kn as PsNode is ast->nodes at (kc - 1)
    var vn as PsNode is ast->nodes at (vc - 1)
    var ti as int is calling token_index_at with tokens, kn.end
    while ti < tokens.len:
        var t as Token is tokens at ti
        if t.start >= vn.start:
            return
        if t.kind == TokKeyword and t.kw == KwTo:
            calling add_edit with es, kn.end, t.end, ","
            return
        if t.kind == TokComma:
            return
        set ti is ti + 1

## Recolecta las ediciones de un AST.
##
## ## Memoria
## Añade ediciones a `es`.
weave collect_edits with ast as ref to PsAst, tokens as vector of Token, text as string, es as ref to vector of MigrateEdit into void:
    var i as int is 0
    var n as int is ast->nodes.len
    while i < n:
        var node as PsNode is ast->nodes at i
        if node.kind == NodeKind.NdListType or node.kind == NodeKind.NdListInitExpr:
            calling rename_head with text, tokens, node.start, "list", "vector", es
        else if node.kind == NodeKind.NdSliceType:
            calling rename_head with text, tokens, node.start, "slice", "span", es
        else if node.kind == NodeKind.NdMapType or node.kind == NodeKind.NdMapInitExpr:
            calling convert_map_sep with ast, tokens, i, es
        set i is i + 1

## Renombra identificadores retirados (`nasci` -> `born`, etc.).
##
## Son palabras que hoy no usa nadie: el renombrado es seguro byte a byte.
##
## ## Memoria
## Añade ediciones.
weave collect_renames with tokens as vector of Token, text as string, es as ref to vector of MigrateEdit into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < tokens.len:
        var t as Token is tokens at i
        if t.kind == TokIdentifier:
            var w as string is (text at t.start to t.end)
            if w == "nasci":
                calling add_edit with es, t.start, t.end, "born"
            else if w == "mori":
                calling add_edit with es, t.start, t.end, "die"
            else if w == "imago":
                calling add_edit with es, t.start, t.end, "mirror"
            else if w == "namespace":
                calling add_edit with es, t.start, t.end, "regnum"
        set i is i + 1

## Aplica las ediciones ordenadas a `text`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string owned.
weave apply_edits with text as string, es as ref to vector of MigrateEdit into string:
    calling sort_edits with es
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    var cursor as int is 0
    var i as int is 0
    while i < es->len:
        var e as MigrateEdit is es at i
        if e.start > cursor:
            calling sb.append with (text at cursor to e.start)
        calling sb.append with e.text
        set cursor is e.end
        set i is i + 1
    if cursor < text length:
        calling sb.append with (text at cursor to (text length))
    return calling sb.finish

## Migra un texto completo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve `MigrateOutcome` owned; liberar con `banish`.
weave migrate_text with text as string into MigrateOutcome:
    var copy_text as string is calling copy with text
    var src as SourceFile is calling SourceFile.from_text with "<migrate>", copy_text
    var bag as diag.DiagnosticBag is calling diag_compat.new_diagnostic_bag
    calling bag.add_source with "<migrate>", (calling src.get_text)
    var kw as KeywordTable is calling pstoken.keyword_table_new
    var lopt as LexOptions is calling psstate.default_lex_options
    var lex as LexResult is calling pslexer.lex with (sigil of src), (sigil of bag), (sigil of kw), lopt
    banish kw
    var popt as PsParseOptions is calling pstate.ps_default_parse_options
    var pr as PsParseResult is calling papi.ps_parse_file with (sigil of src), (sigil of bag), (sigil of lex), popt
    var es as vector of MigrateEdit is vector of MigrateEdit
    if pr.ok:
        calling collect_edits with (sigil of pr.ast), lex.tokens, copy_text, (sigil of es)
        calling collect_renames with lex.tokens, copy_text, (sigil of es)
    var changes as int is es.len
    var okp as bool is pr.ok
    var out_text as string is ""
    if changes > 0:
        set out_text is calling apply_edits with copy_text, (sigil of es)
    else:
        set out_text is calling copy with text
    banish es
    banish pr
    banish bag
    banish src
    banish copy_text
    return with text is out_text, changes is changes, ok is okp

## Implementa `psc migrate`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera el ParseResult y los textos.
weave run_migrate with args as vector of string into int:
    var sf as vector of string is vector of string
    calling sf.push with "--check"
    calling sf.push with "--diff"
    calling sf.push with "--verbose"
    calling sf.push with "--help"
    var pr as cliargs.ParseResult is calling cliargs.parse with args, 2, vector of string, sf, vector of string
    if not pr.ok:
        var e as string is pr.error
        calling spark.eprintln with e
        calling cliargs.free_parse_result with (sigil of pr)
        return 2
    if calling cliargs.enabled with (sigil of pr.args), "--help":
        calling print_help
        calling cliargs.free_parse_result with (sigil of pr)
        return 0
    var check_only as bool is calling cliargs.enabled with (sigil of pr.args), "--check"
    var show_diff as bool is calling cliargs.enabled with (sigil of pr.args), "--diff"
    var verbose as bool is calling cliargs.enabled with (sigil of pr.args), "--verbose"
    var changed as int is 0
    var failed as int is 0
    var pi as int is 0
    while pi < pr.args.positionals.len:
        var p as string is (pr.args.positionals at pi)
        var files as vector of string is vector of string
        if calling archivum.is_dir with p:
            var found as vector of string is calling archivum.find_files with p, true
            for f in found:
                if calling ends_with with f, ".pengu":
                    calling files.push with (calling copy with f)
                banish f
            banish found
        else:
            calling files.push with (calling copy with p)
        var fi as int is 0
        while fi < files.len:
            var f as string is (files at fi)
            var txtm as maybe string is calling archivum.read_text with f
            if txtm.is_present:
                var original as string is txtm.value
                var mo as MigrateOutcome is calling migrate_text with original
                if not mo.ok:
                    set failed is failed + 1
                    var fm as string is "cannot parse {f}: skipped"
                    calling spark.eprintln with fm
                    banish fm
                else if mo.changes > 0:
                    set changed is changed + 1
                    if verbose or check_only:
                        var hm as string is "{f}: {mo.changes} change(s)"
                        calling spark.println with hm
                        banish hm
                    if show_diff:
                        calling print_edits with f, original, mo.text
                    if not check_only and not show_diff:
                        var okw as bool is calling archivum.write_text with f, mo.text
                        if not okw:
                            var em as string is "cannot write {f}"
                            calling spark.eprintln with em
                            banish em
                banish mo
            banish txtm
            banish f
            set fi is fi + 1
        banish files
        set pi is pi + 1
    if check_only or show_diff:
        var cm as string is "{changed} file(s) would be migrated."
        calling spark.println with cm
        banish cm
    else:
        var dm as string is "{changed} file(s) migrated."
        calling spark.println with dm
        banish dm
    if failed > 0:
        var xm as string is "{failed} file(s) skipped (parse errors)."
        calling spark.eprintln with xm
        banish xm
    calling cliargs.free_parse_result with (sigil of pr)
    if check_only and changed > 0:
        return 1
    if failed > 0:
        return 2
    return 0

## Imprime las líneas que cambian entre `old` y `new`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera las listas de líneas.
weave print_edits with path as string, old as string, new as string into void:
    var hm as string is "--- {path}"
    calling spark.println with hm
    banish hm
    var oldl as vector of string is calling old.split with "\n"
    var newl as vector of string is calling new.split with "\n"
    var i as int is 0
    var n as int is oldl.len
    if newl.len > n:
        set n is newl.len
    while i < n:
        var ov as string is ""
        var nv as string is ""
        if i < oldl.len:
            set ov is (oldl at i)
        if i < newl.len:
            set nv is (newl at i)
        if ov != nv:
            var om as string is "- {ov}"
            calling spark.println with om
            banish om
            var nm as string is "+ {nv}"
            calling spark.println with nm
            banish nm
        set i is i + 1
    banish newl
    banish oldl
